\n### 3. Commands with TestSIGPIPE Tests (25+ found)\n\nFiles with SIGPIPE tests: arch, b2sum, base32, basenc, cat, cksum, comm, du, md5sum, mkfifo, mknod, nice, nl, nohup, pathchk, sha1sum, sha224sum, sha256sum, sha384sum, sha512sum, sum, tac, tsort, unexpand, uniq, yes\n\n### 4. SIGPIPE Handler Implementation\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5611/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`:\n\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n\tgo func() {\n\t\t<-c\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}()\n}\n```\n\nThis is called at the start of main() in affected commands and ensures exit 0 when stdout/stderr is closed by a downstream consumer (matching GNU coreutils behavior).\n\n### 5. Helper Functions in pkg/testutils/\n\nLocated in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5611/pkg/testutils/`:\n\n- **BuildBinary()**: Compiles Go package and returns binary path (in build.go)\n- **RunDiffTests()**: Executes differential tests comparing Go and reference binaries (in difftest.go)\n- **ComposeNormalizers()**: Combines multiple NormalizeFunc functions (in difftest.go)\n- **TimestampNormalizer**: Built-in normalizer for timestamp patterns (in difftest.go)\n\nNote: The DiffTest struct is used for **differential testing** (comparing Go vs GNU implementations), NOT for SIGPIPE-specific testing. SIGPIPE tests are custom integration tests that use exec.StdoutPipe() directly to simulate the broken pipe condition."}],"totalDurationMs":55750,"totalTokens":55262,"totalToolUseCount":22,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":52042,"output_tokens":2516,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":699},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":2516,"cache_read_input_t